## Code Quality Standards

### 1. Complexity Limits
- **Cyclomatic complexity**: Max 10 per function
- **Function length**: Max 50 lines (extract helpers if longer)
- **Parameters**: Max 4 parameters (use object parameter if more)
- **Nesting depth**: Max 3 levels (extract functions to reduce)

### 2. Extraction Guidelines
```typescript
// ❌ BAD: Too long, too many parameters
function processOrder(userId: string, items: Item[], discount: number, tax: number, shipping: number) {
  // 80 lines of code
}

// ✅ GOOD: Extracted, object parameter
function processOrder(order: ProcessOrderParams): OrderResult {
  const subtotal = calculateSubtotal(order.items);
  const discountAmount = applyDiscount(subtotal, order.discount);
  const taxAmount = calculateTax(discountAmount, order.tax);
  return createOrder({ ...order, subtotal, discountAmount, taxAmount });
}
```

### 3. Function Extraction Triggers
Extract a function when:
- Function exceeds 50 lines
- Code is repeated 2+ times
- Logic can be tested independently
- Function does multiple things (violates single responsibility)

